<title>GERMANY: TABLE-HOECHST DETAILS H1 97 RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TABLE-HOECHST DETAILS H1 97 RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30 1997</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   743     vs 1,836</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     2,003   vs 4,320</p>
<p>    Group operating profit		   2,270   vs 2,775</p>
<p>Of which</p>
<p>     Europe					1,148   vs 1,629</p>
<p>     Americas				    994     vs 944</p>
<p>     Asia, Africa, Australasia	     128     vs 228</p>
<p>    Group income before minorities	 1,008   vs 2,209</p>
<p>    Group sales				  27,886  vs 26,091</p>
<p>By origin</p>
<p>     Europe (incl. Germany)		  16,241  vs 15,050</p>
<p>     Americas				    10,679  vs 9,759</p>
<p>     Asia, Africa, Australasia	     3,212   vs 2,830</p>
<p>     Intragroup sales			  -2,246  vs -1,548</p>
<p>By destination</p>
<p>     Europe					13,294  vs 13,089</p>
<p>     Of which Germany			  4,583   vs 4,681</p>
<p>     Americas				    9,962   vs 8,886</p>
<p>     Asia, Africa, Australasia	     4,630   vs 4,107</p>
<p>Capital expenditure on tangible</p>
<p>    and intangible fixed assets	    1,795   vs 1,723</p>
<p>    Personnel expenses			 6,904   vs 6,469</p>
<p>    No of employees (June 30)		145,556 vs 147,058</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of German chemical group is Hoechst AG. The group said that pretax profits and sales declined in the first half of the year because of the absence of extraordinary gains from disposals.</p>
<p>The company gave the following figures on a comparable basis, ie, after eliminating the extraordinary items included in the first half of 1996.</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Comparable operating profit	    2,640   vs 2,478</p>
<p>    Comparable pretax profit		 2,575   vs 2,346</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
